# {{name}}

A Pterodactyl panel theme of CSS alone, scaffolded by `p:extension:make --theme --css-only`. Level 1 of
the themes guide, `node_modules/@pterodactyl/sdk/THEMES.md`, covers it: colours, fonts, radius and
spacing, for dark and light. Skins and views (levels 2 to 4) need a theme scaffolded without `--css-only`.

## Files

| File | |
| --- | --- |
| `extension.json` | The manifest. `"type": "theme"` and its `theme` section declare the stylesheet, the colour schemes and the settings. |
| `src/theme.css` | The panel stylesheet with this theme's tokens and classes. Plain Tailwind, no prefix. |

## Scripts

| Script | |
| --- | --- |
| `npm run build` | `dist/theme.css` and `dist/theme.json`. |
| `npm run dev` | Rebuilds on change; `p:extension:dev --watch` runs it. |
| `npm run doctor` | The panel's checks: manifest, build, budgets and remote URLs. |
| `npm run pack` | Packs a `.pteroext` archive to install on another panel. |

## Develop

```sh
npm install
php {{artisan}} p:extension:dev . --enable
php {{artisan}} p:theme:activate {{id}}
php {{artisan}} p:extension:dev . --watch
```

The first command builds, installs and enables the theme. While the last one runs on a panel with
`APP_DEBUG=true`, a change to `src/theme.css` swaps into open pages without a reload.
